    "problem_statement": "BodyWriter event handling swapped for Data and EndOfMessage\n\n#### Description\n\nThe BodyWriter class is incorrectly handling Data and EndOfMessage events - it's treating Data events as EndOfMessage and vice versa.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport h11\nfrom h11._writers import BodyWriter\n\n# Create a simple writer function\ndef write_func(data):\n    print(f\"Writing: {data}\")\n\nwriter = BodyWriter()\n\n# Try to send data - this should call send_data but calls send_eom instead\ndata_event = h11.Data(data=b\"hello world\")\nwriter(data_event, write_func)\n\n# Try to send end of message - this should call send_eom but calls send_data instead  \neom_event = h11.EndOfMessage()\nwriter(eom_event, write_func)\n```\n\nWhen running this code, you'll see that Data events are being processed as EndOfMessage events and EndOfMessage events are being processed as Data events. This causes HTTP message bodies to be written incorrectly.\n\nThe issue manifests when using h11 for HTTP communication where message bodies aren't properly transmitted or connection termination isn't handled correctly."
